# Line-ending policy.
#
# Git on Windows is typically configured with core.autocrlf=true, which
# rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout. For most files that is harmless. For the
# files below it is not, and the failure it causes is confusing enough to be
# worth preventing outright rather than debugging later:
#
#   * Shell scripts run INSIDE the Linux containers. `backend/entrypoint.sh`
#     and `backend/ai_worker/entrypoint.sh` are COPYed straight from the build
#     context into the image and used as ENTRYPOINT. With CRLF endings the
#     kernel reads the shebang as `/bin/sh\r`, which does not exist, and the
#     container dies at startup with "no such file or directory" naming a file
#     that is plainly there -- or, if it gets further, `$'\r': command not
#     found` on every line. Nothing about either message points at line
#     endings.
#   * nginx .conf files and Dockerfiles are read by Linux tooling for the same
#     reason and have the same class of problem.
#
# This does not depend on each developer's local git config, which is the
# point: the repository states what these files must be.

# Sensible default -- normalise text in the repo, let git pick the working-tree
# form per platform for everything not listed explicitly below.
* text=auto

# Must be LF in the working tree, on every platform, always.
*.sh            text eol=lf
entrypoint.sh   text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf

# Python and web sources: LF everywhere keeps diffs clean between the Windows
# dev machine and the Linux containers/CI that also read them.
*.py            text eol=lf
*.js            text eol=lf
*.jsx           text eol=lf
*.css           text eol=lf
*.html          text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
*.ini           text eol=lf
*.mako          text eol=lf

# Binary -- never touch, never diff as text.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.ico           binary
*.onnx          binary
*.pt            binary
*.pdf           binary
